WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.388
Coding Exercise 3 asks you to build a searched CASE
with clear

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.012
boundaries Begin with an explicit NULL branch Then
add exact zero

00:00:09.038 --> 00:00:13.775
as No Charge Next add the high-value threshold and
the standard threshold

00:00:13.925 --> 00:00:19.075
in that order Use ELSE for the remaining known
positive bills The

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:23.200
order matters because CASE stops at the first true
branch The NULL

00:00:23.225 --> 00:00:27.850
branch preserves missingness as Unknown rather than
classifying it as low The

00:00:27.875 --> 00:00:32.700
zero branch separates a no-charge state from a
low-value charge After running

00:00:32.875 --> 00:00:38.825
inspect patient 103 patient 107 patient 101 and
patient 102

00:00:39.712 --> 00:00:42.562
Those records exercise the main branches of the rule
